    "result_text": "All test files are accounted for \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class, and it passes along with the full build. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `customerCode` format was changed from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence).\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the single place that generates the code:\n- Added a `CITY3` prefix (upper-cased first three letters of the city).\n- Changed the sequence from a global count (`findAll().size() + 1`) to a **per-city** count \u2014 filtering `findAll()` by matching city (case-insensitively, consistent with the case-insensitive prefix) and adding one. Since this step runs before `SaveOwner`, the count correctly excludes the owner being created.\n- Extracted a small `prefix(String)` helper so the CITY3 and LAST3 logic isn't duplicated.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipNumber` is formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it **rebuilds automatically** on the new format (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`); no logic change was needed, only the Javadoc example was corrected. It was the only value derived from `customerCode`.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
